How Flask projects usually flow (mental map)

1. App factory & extensions → create the Flask app and plug in tools (DB, CSRF, etc.).

2. Blueprints (routes/views) → group related routes (e.g., core, recipes, ingredients).

3. Templates → Jinja HTML files for each view (inherit from base.html).

4. Models → Python classes that map to DB tables.

5. Forms → WTForms classes and validation.

6. CRUD → views + forms + templates wired to models.

7. Migrations → track schema changes safely.

You’ll repeat a tiny loop for each feature:

Model → Register (import/blueprint) → View (route logic) → Template (HTML) → Test

5) Initialize migrations (structure only)

